From: Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build/rust: keep Crubit off when there is no rust_crubit_root

M158 reduced `enable_cpp_api_from_rust` to `enable_rust &&
build_with_chromium`.  M157 also required `use_chromium_rust_toolchain` and
`!rust_prebuilt_stdlib`, so with a system Rust sysroot (rust_sysroot_absolute)
the flag was false, and every Crubit consumer fell back to its cxx path or was
skipped.  Now the flag is true for the system toolchain too, and the first
consumer, //build/rust/std's prebuilt_{core,alloc,std}_bindings, dies in
gn gen:

  ERROR at //build/rust/gni_impl/cpp_api_from_rust.gni:64:3: Assertion failed.
    assert(rust_crubit_root != "", rust_crubit_root_missing_message)

`rust_crubit_root` (new in M158) is "" unless use_chromium_rust_toolchain is
set or the caller names a Crubit build, and a distribution Rust ships no
cc_bindings_from_rs.  Requiring a root restores the M157 behaviour for that
case and changes nothing for the bundled toolchain, where rust.gni defaults the
root to //third_party/rust-toolchain.  The *-crubit patches in this package
rely on the flag being false.

Applied only with USE=-bundled-toolchain.  Drop it once Crubit can be built for
the system Rust toolchain (it needs a rustc-dev from the same rustc build).

diff -ruN a/build/config/rust.gni b/build/config/rust.gni
--- a/build/config/rust.gni	2026-11-18 15:33:16.564091613 -0300
+++ b/build/config/rust.gni	2026-11-18 15:33:16.579542571 -0300
@@ -454,7 +454,11 @@
 #
 # See the `assert` comments in `cpp_api_from_rust.gni` for explanation of
 # the conditions used here.
-enable_cpp_api_from_rust = enable_rust && build_with_chromium
+# bentoo: also require a Crubit root.  M158 dropped the toolchain conditions
+# M157 had here, so a custom `rust_sysroot_absolute` without Crubit asserts in
+# cpp_api_from_rust.gni instead of falling back to the cxx paths.
+enable_cpp_api_from_rust =
+    enable_rust && build_with_chromium && rust_crubit_root != ""
 
 declare_args() {
   # Whether it is okay to use `rust_api_from_cpp.gni`.  The default is `false`,
